      "body": "Stack (5/6), merge in order: [#44851](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/44851) → [#44852](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/44852) → [#44853](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/44853) → [#44854](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/44854) → [#44863](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/44863) → [#44869](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/44869)\n\nKernel capability detection currently reports `cpu` when Intel XPU is the available accelerator. Add `DeviceType.XPU` and `CapabilityRequirement.XPU`, and detect XPU after the existing accelerator checks. This lets the inventory describe XPU kernels and excludes XPU processes from CPU-only capabilities.\n\nValidation on an Intel Arc Pro B70 with PyTorch 2.13.0+xpu:\n\n- 123 namespace and fused-op dispatch tests passed across three separate test processes.\n- Four Gemma4 XPU serving tests passed, covering one-step and three-step captured MTP.\n- The new detection regression fails on the previous source. The patched hardware probe reports `xpu` with XPU available.\n- Pre-commit checks passed.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #39011238691](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39011238691)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39011238678](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39011238678)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39011238701](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39011238701)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
