            },
            "body": "Forwarding @mingfeima’s review of this source patch in weekly consolidation #46623 so the fixes land in the original PR. @alexnails, please address the outstanding items here, validate the updated tests, and link the source fix back to the consolidation review:\n\n1. **Keep the existing test-fixture style** in `test/registered/unit/kernels/test_kernels_namespace.py`. Mingfei suggested:\n   ```python\n   _MUSA = PlatformInfo(device_type=\"musa\")\n   _XPU = PlatformInfo(device_type=\"xpu\")\n   ```\n   Original feedback: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/46623#discussion_r4386272531\n2. **Cover XPU capability matching in the existing parameterized `test_capability_is_satisfied_by` test.** His follow-up: “cover XPU capability matching in the parameterized test from `test_capability_is_satisfied_by`”.\n   Original feedback: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/46623#discussion_r4386282859\n\nFor completeness, his earlier enum suggestion was to retain `XPU = \"xpu\"` and remove the trailing TODO in `python/sglang/kernels/spec.py`: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/46623#discussion_r4385511573 . That suggestion is already applied and the thread is resolved in #46623; please carry the same cleanup in the source PR so future replays preserve it.\n\nThe two test requests remain unresolved in the consolidation. Source authors retain ownership of the fixes; forwarding this feedback does not resolve the original review threads.",
